L254 -- the kinematic Sunyaev-Zel'dovich pairwise velocity as a test of who does the clustering

LITERATURE BLOCK (quoted values, not recomputed here)
    pairwise kSZ detection 3.8 sigma  --  Hand et al. 2012, PRL 109 041101 (arXiv:1203.4219), ACT x BOSS -- first detection
    pairwise kSZ detection 4.2 sigma  --  Soergel et al. 2016, MNRAS 461 3172 (arXiv:1603.03904), SPT-SZ x DES-Y1 clusters
    pairwise kSZ detection 3.8 sigma  --  De Bernardis et al. 2017, JCAP 03 008 (arXiv:1607.02139), ACT x BOSS DR11
    pairwise kSZ detection 5.4 sigma  --  Calafut et al. 2021, PRD 104 043502 (arXiv:2101.08374), ACT DR5+Planck x SDSS DR15 LRG
    stacked   kSZ detection 6.5 sigma  --  Schaan et al. 2021, PRD 103 063513 (arXiv:2009.05557), ACT DR5 x BOSS, velocity-reconstruction stacking (NOT pairwise)
    sigma_tau/tau = 15%  --  Battaglia 2016, JCAP 08 058 (arXiv:1607.02442) 'The tau of galaxy clusters': optical-depth uncertainty ~15% for Planck-like cluster samples; sub-grid physics systematics <10% when a tau-tSZ relation is used
    sigma_tau/tau = 30%  --  Amodeo et al. 2021, PRD 103 063514 (arXiv:2009.05558) and the feedback literature that followed it: hydrodynamic simulations under-predict the measured kSZ/tSZ gas profiles, and strong- vs weak-feedback models differ by tens of percent
    sigma_tau/tau = 10%  --  optimistic floor if the gas profile is externally calibrated

